"<!-- Created by firescale (group-project/pr-template). It is your team's to edit. -->

## What this changes

<!-- One or two sentences. Link the issue it closes, for example: Closes #12 -->

## How to test it

<!-- The steps a reviewer can follow to see it work. -->

## Checklist

- [ ] \`npx firescale verify\` passes on my machine.
- [ ] The branch is named as CONTRIBUTING.md says.
- [ ] Tests cover the change, or I wrote above why they do not.
- [ ] A teammate is asked to review.
"
`;

exports[`fscale init --packs core,group-project > writes the commands of each project into the guide > CONTRIBUTING.md of the course project 1`] = `
"# Contributing

<!-- Created by firescale (group-project/contributing). It is your team's to edit. -->

How we work on this repo together. Read it before your first pull request.

## Set up

Install the dependencies. Run each command in the folder it names:

- In \`backend/audit_service\`: \`python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt\`
- In \`backend/auth_service\`: \`python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt\`
- In \`backend/ledger_service\`: \`python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt\`
- In \`backend/market_service\`: \`python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt\`
- In \`backend/realtime_service\`: \`python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt\`
- In \`frontend\`: \`npm install\`

For a Python project, first make a virtual environment in its folder and activate it: \`python -m venv .venv\`. \`fscale verify\` uses the \`.venv\` in a project's folder by itself.

## Check your work

Before you push, run the same check that CI runs:

\`\`\`sh
npx firescale verify
\`\`\`

It runs the firescale rules, then lint, typecheck and tests in every project. Fix what it reports before you ask for a review. When it says \`SETUP NEEDED\`, your machine is missing something: run the command it shows, and do not change code for it.

To run one step on its own, run its command in that folder:

| Folder | Lint | Typecheck | Test |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| \`backend/audit_service\` | - | - | \`python -m pytest\` |
| \`backend/auth_service\` | \`python -m ruff check .\` | - | \`python -m pytest\` |
| \`backend/ledger_service\` | - | - | \`python -m pytest\` |
| \`backend/market_service\` | - | - | \`python -m pytest\` |
| \`backend/realtime_service\` | - | - | \`python -m pytest\` |
| \`frontend\` | \`npx --no oxlint\` | \`npx --no tsc --noEmit\` | - |

## Branches

Do not commit to the main branch directly. Make a branch for each change, with a name that matches one of these patterns (\`*\` is any text):

- \`feat/*\`
- \`fix/*\`
- \`docs/*\`
- \`test/*\`
- \`refactor/*\`
- \`chore/*\`
- \`ci/*\`
- \`build/*\`
- \`perf/*\`
- \`style/*\`
- \`release/*\`
- \`hotfix/*\`
- \`revert/*\`

The long-lived branches are \`main\`, \`master\`, \`develop\`.

For example: \`git switch -c feat/login-page\`.

## Pull requests

- Keep each pull request to one change, small enough to review in one sitting.
- Fill in the pull request template.
- CI runs \`npx firescale verify\`. It must pass before the pull request is merged.
- A teammate reviews and approves it before it is merged.
"
`;
